# Planbook has no build, so there is nothing generated to ignore. Everything below is
# machine noise or local scratch.

# OS cruft
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Local scratch — anything you don't intend to keep goes in one of these
scratch/
scratchpad/
*.local.*
*.log

# Deliberately NOT ignored: .claude/dispatch/.
# It looks like agent scratch and it is not. Each work order leaves a <WO-ID>-brief.md (what was
# asked) and a <WO-ID>-result.md (what came back) — together the audit trail for why a work order
# was routed where it was and what the implementer actually claimed. A work order questioned in
# February needs both halves, and the chat transcript that held the second half will be gone.
# It will grow to ~40 file pairs by Phase 8; that is a few hundred KB of plain text, which is a
# cheap price for a decision record.

# Deliberately NOT ignored: package.json, package-lock.json, node_modules/.
# They cannot legitimately exist here (no dependencies, no bundler — see CLAUDE.md), and an
# ignore rule would hide one from `git status` instead of surfacing it. If one appears,
# delete it; don't ignore it. Anything scripted lives in tools/*.mjs under bare Node.
